{{~ if project["backend.topology"] == "services" ~}}
## External MCP servers

The services use external MCP servers. Declare each one in `src/AppHost/AppHost.cs`, on the service hosts, never on the edge or in a module: its parameters before the loop over `builder.ServiceHosts()`, since a parameter is declared once, and the server on `service` inside the loop, so every service host can call it:

```csharp
var docsUrl = builder.AddParameter("mcp-docs-url");
var docsToken = builder.AddParameter("mcp-docs-token", secret: true);
var filesCommand = builder.AddParameter("mcp-files-command");

foreach (var (module, project) in builder.ServiceHosts())
{
    // ...
    service.WithMcpServerUrl("docs", docsUrl, docsToken)
        .WithMcpServerCommand("files", filesCommand, ["--root", "/data"]);
    // ...
}
```

The edge runs no module code, so the AppHost refuses a server declared on it. Give the parameters values in the AppHost's user secrets (`dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:mcp-docs-url https://... --project src/AppHost`), never in a committed file. Code calls the tools through `IMcpTools`; `tests/Mcp.Tests` shows both kinds of server against a tiny one of its own, declared on every service host.
{{~ else ~}}
## External MCP servers

The host uses external MCP servers. Declare each one on the host in `src/AppHost/AppHost.cs`, never in a module:

```csharp
host.WithMcpServerUrl("docs", builder.AddParameter("mcp-docs-url"), builder.AddParameter("mcp-docs-token", secret: true));
host.WithMcpServerCommand("files", builder.AddParameter("mcp-files-command"), ["--root", "/data"]);
```

Give the parameters values in the AppHost's user secrets (`dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:mcp-docs-url https://... --project src/AppHost`), never in a committed file. Code calls the tools through `IMcpTools`; `tests/Mcp.Tests` shows both kinds of server against a tiny one of its own.
{{~ end ~}}